implementationPlan.description:
Regenerate the vendored copy and apply its hunks with Edit (mem:gotcha-moe-doc-generated-artifacts, mem:convention-docs-vendored-regen-gate).

Regenerate in a snapshot outside the shared checkout, never in place. Never run npm run build or prebuild anywhere in the shared tree (global rail). Example: `S=$(mktemp -d); git archive HEAD | tar -x -C $S; cp --parents docs/skills/{moe-planning,ponytail}/SKILL.md $S`. Then in $S/packages/moe-daemon, under env -i with the nvm Node v24.21.0 bin on PATH, run `npm ci && npm run -s generate-skill-files`. It must print 'Generated ... (65 skill files across 17 skills)'. A 'skipping' line means docs/ was missing, not success. This generator hashes content only and needs no git history, so an archive is enough.

Diff the regenerated skillFiles.ts against the tracked packages/moe-daemon/src/generated/skillFiles.ts. Expect exactly 4 hunks, the same as the architect's /mnt/d/moe-scratch/plan-d60a0109/skillFiles.regen.diff:
- the moe-planning/SKILL.md entry's '# moe-generated: sha=' marker (a2881f92c874 -> 247fee8eaf61 for the prototype's bytes);
- its Size-triage line;
- the ponytail/SKILL.md entry's marker (ad8f5eeab200 -> 22cebfcbaa64);
- its footer lines.
If your step-1 bytes differ from the prototype at all, the shas differ: always take them from your own regeneration, never compute or copy them by hand.

Apply each hunk to the tracked file with the Edit tool. The file is about 1.36 MB (30,910 lines), too big for Write, and cp is a shell write with no TOOL witness. Read only the lines around each hunk (offset/limit, near 1269-1290 and 1490-1635), then Edit with an old_string unique in the file. The template literal escapes backticks as \`, exactly as the generator wrote them.

Verification. Run it once, before moe.complete_task; its fresh output is the completion evidence. From the task worktree root, run the executionContract checkRef exactly as written. The same text (918 chars) is at /mnt/d/moe-scratch/plan-d60a0109/checkref-gate.txt.

What it does:
- the DoD-1 grep (no 'distinct affectedFiles' left under docs/skills);
- two positive greps for the new wording;
- a whole-tree `git archive HEAD` snapshot outside the repo, with the three owned files overlaid.

Then, under env -i with nvm Node v24.21.0, in that snapshot:
- `npm run -s lint` at the snapshot root (DoD 3);
- `npm ci`, then sha1sum skillFiles.ts, `npm run -s generate-skill-files | grep Generated`, and `sha1sum -c` (DoD 2: the hand-applied hunks are byte-identical to the generator's output);
- `npx vitest run src/util/skillFiles.test.ts`.

The architect's dry run at 9224de15:
- with the prototype and its regenerated skillFiles.ts: lint OK (architect.md 39, worker.md 30, qa.md 36 lines), 'Generated ...', 'Test Files 1 passed (1)', 'Tests 11 passed (11)', exit 0;
- negative control, the stale tracked skillFiles.ts: 'src/generated/skillFiles.ts: FAILED', exit 1.

Also confirm `git diff --stat` lists only the three owned files (DoD 3).
